    },
    "message": "Provision generated Scenarios to the planning standard by default\n\nGenerated Scenarios now get facilities, staff and supplies sized to\nthe planning standard or the modeled demand, whichever is larger:\n\n- Toilets: the larger of accessible toilets plus one per 50 people and\n  the units 5 uses per person per day need within the target load.\n- Water and meal stations: units that keep the default coefficients'\n  daily demand within the target load, each a separate facility since\n  a floor-plan facility serves one person at a time.\n- Staff: general staff as before plus one station-based staff member\n  per station in the food zone, where water and meal service need them.\n  An entered total keeps at least one general staff member.\n- Supplies: with no entered inventory, three days of 3 L drinking water\n  and three meal units per person, then the same amount daily from day\n  4 (default_supply_start_day). Entered inventories are kept.\n\nRegion-condition deliveries now carry a shipment ID; without it a\npending delivery stopped the Run at the first state validation. The\ncapacity diagnostic counts a floor-plan facility as one unit, matching\nphysical_service_capacity. Sources and assumptions are registered in\nthe manifest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
